// From the law: RA 8491 Section 27, width 1, length 2, triangle's sides 1. Executive Order 23
// of 1936, with W = 90:
//   sun's diameter D = W/5 = 18; major beam R = 5/9 D = 10; minor beam r = 4/5 R = 8
//   eight rays, ray arc = free arc, so 22.5 degrees each; major beam twice a minor's breadth
//   stars: outer diameter 5/9 D = 10, inner 2/9 D = 4, one point at the corner, D/2 = 9
//   from it, so each center is 14 along the corner's bisector (reading the distance as
//   measured to the star's tip)
// The triangle's altitude is 90 sin 60 = 77.9423 (derived). The three rotations are the
// bisectors' angles (derived). Not from the law: the sun's center, 28 from the hoist.
vexyl 1
meta {
  name "Philippines"
  encoder "Naomi Persephone Amethyst"
  license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
  adapted-from "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Philippines.svg" {
    author "Wikimedia Commons contributors, listed in the file's history"
    license "LicenseRef-Public-Domain"
    part "the outlines of the sun's beams"
  }
  source "https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1998/ra_8491_1998.html"
  source "https://web.archive.org/web/20230127120252/https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/1936/03/25/executive-order-no-23-s-1936/"
  source "https://www.crwflags.com/fotw/flags/ph.html"
  source "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Philippines_(construction_sheet).svg"
  note "The Order's illustration wasn't seen, so the sun's center isn't from the law: 28 from the hoist is the Commons construction sheet's value, where the triangle's centroid would be 25.98. The outlines of the beams, including the gaps between them and their pointed ends, also come from the Commons file, because the law gives only their lengths and relative breadth."
  note "The Order's distance of D/2 from each corner is read as reaching the star's tip, as the Commons sheet does. Measured to the star's center, the star wouldn't fit inside the triangle."
  note "The law gives colors as Cable numbers. The Pantone and CMYK values are the Album des Pavillons 2000's, as FOTW reports them. No reliable screen value was found, so the hex values are the Commons drawing's: the RGB values on FOTW include an impossible orange-red for the yellow, so they were set aside."
  note "Section 10 of RA 8491 puts the red field on top in time of war. Section 34 lists prohibited uses. The canvas edge and fringe in the Order are left out."
  note "The 1987 Constitution's Article XVI wasn't read directly. Its terms are from FOTW's quotation."
  law "1987 Constitution of the Philippines, Article XVI, Section 1"
  law "Republic Act No. 8491, Flag and Heraldic Code of the Philippines, 12 February 1998" {
    source "https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1998/ra_8491_1998.html"
  }
  law "Executive Order No. 23 of 25 March 1936, Description and Specification of the Filipino Flag" {
    source "https://web.archive.org/web/20230127120252/https://www.officialgazette.gov.ph/1936/03/25/executive-order-no-23-s-1936/"
  }
  restriction "Section 34 of RA 8491: among other things, the flag may not be used as a trademark or on industrial, commercial or agricultural labels or designs." {
    source "https://lawphil.net/statutes/repacts/ra1998/ra_8491_1998.html"
  }
}
